# Keep ChatGPT MCP OAuth scopes, PKCE and consent safe

- Public issuer: https://blossom.wenneker.dev ; protected resource: https://blossom.wenneker.dev/mcp.
- Maintain OAuth discovery, PKCE S256, dynamic registration with strict redirect_uri allowlist, state/issuer/resource checks, one-time authorization codes, expiring tokens and least privilege.
- blossom:read is insufficient for writing Studio results or Music DNA; blossom:write must be requested and approved. A scope hint never grants privileges.
- Keep credentials, auth code, state, PKCE verifier, access/refresh tokens and personal data out of logs and reports.
- Distinguish stages: client_registered, consent_shown, consent_denied, consent_redirected, consent_repeated, token_rejected, token_issued, mcp_connected and tools_listed. History matters more than latestStage.
- consent_redirected does not mean ChatGPT exchanged a code. token_issued does not mean tools listed; tools_listed does not mean ChatGPT plugin installed.
- A repeated consent form must never mint another grant. Denied consent should be labelled denied, not approved.
- Never bypass ChatGPT's plugin creation or external account restrictions.
